# Algorithm: UDP Client

1. Start.
2. Declare the client socket, server address structure,
   buffer, port number, and address size.
3. Create a UDP socket using
   socket(AF_INET, SOCK_DGRAM, 0).
4. If socket creation fails, display an error and stop.
5. Read the server port number from the user.
6. Set the server address family to AF_INET.
7. Set the server port using htons(port).
8. Set the server IP address to 127.0.0.1
   using inet_addr().
9. Initialize the address size using sizeof(serverAddr).
10. Copy the message into the buffer using strcpy().
11. Send the message to the server using sendto().
12. Receive the server's reply using recvfrom().
13. Display the received message.
14. Close the socket using close().
15. Stop.



